WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.520
Let's talk about Elizabeth Warren.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:08.820
Uh, 2020 Democratic candidate Elizabeth Warren
has refused an invitation to do a town hall

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.820
on Fox News.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.300
And there's a lot to discuss here.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.039
And, and I'm very interested in many of the
elements that are going on here.

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:21.810
So you might remember that not long ago weeks
was it a couple months times flying, uh, 2020

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:26.680
Democratic candidate Bernie Sanders did a
Fox News town hall and he absolutely crushed

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.680
it.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.990
He had the entire room clapping for Medicare
for all.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:36.400
He schooled the moderators, Martha Maccallum
and Bret Baier on everything from healthcare

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.050
to taxes to economics.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.520
I mean, really just everything.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.180
It went really, really well for Bernie Sanders
and it went really poorly for Fox News.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.710
Elizabeth Warren has been invited to do her
own town hall on Fox News and she's taking

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.710
a different approach.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:56.899
She is turned it down and she says, Fox News
is a hate for profit racket that gives a megaphone

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:02.640
to racists and conspiracists, which of course
is completely true, but there's still a question

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:10.509
of whether Elizabeth Warren might benefit
in the net by appearing on Fox News and talking

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:15.340
about what are mostly very good ideas that
she has as compared to ignoring Fox News all

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.340
together.

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.340
Now, this is so funny.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.040
There are people attacking me on Twitter already.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.670
Like I haven't even commented on the Elizabeth
Warren Fox News town hall thing.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.469
I'm, I'm commenting on it now and people are
tweeting me saying, David, you are going to

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:34.570
be a hypocrite because you praised Bernie
Sanders for doing the town hall, and you're

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.049
going to praise Elizabeth Warren for not doing
the town hall.

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:43.600
But remember what I said when Bernie did the
town hall is I think that there are two legitimate

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.079
perspectives here.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:50.109
Do the town hall knowing that Fox News is
the propaganda arm of the Trump administration

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:54.909
because you're making the calculation that
you'd rather reach some portion of their audience

00:01:54.909 --> 00:01:56.789
that is convincible.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:01.280
Even though it's a total hate for profit racket,
as Elizabeth Warren points out, that's a legitimate

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.380
idea, legitimate point of view.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:09.130
It's also legitimate to say, I'm not going
to implicitly or explicitly give attention

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:14.380
to this propaganda network, nor allow them
to use me, uh, to continue their hate for

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.850
profit racket.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.400
Both are legitimate, but you don't have to
take my word for it.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.140
Let's actually look at what I said the day
I covered the Bernie Sanders town hall.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.090
But there were sort of two main arguments
leading up to this about whether Bernie Sanders

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.650
should or shouldn't appear.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:32.950
The argument against Bernie appearing is a
very simple one, which is Fox News is the

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.670
propaganda arm of the Trump administration.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:43.940
It is not going to be, uh, a town hall that
is a sort of fairly set up.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:49.140
It is going to be an audience that is going
to have a hand pick people from political

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.710
groups including turning point USA, which
happened.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:57.870
It's going to be one that most likely will
turn into a two on one sort of argument between

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:01.680
two Fox News moderators and Bernie Sanders,
which it did.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.030
And uh, it's a net loss.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.070
Don't give them the ratings by appearing.

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.730
That was the argument against Bernie appearing
on the other side.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:14.170
The argument for Bernie appearing, uh, is
listen, these are people who otherwise may

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:19.180
never even get a real understanding from Bernie
himself about what his policies are.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:23.570
Most people, not in the physical audience,
but in the Fox News television audience probably

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.760
are not going to be voting for the Democrat
in November of 2020.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.190
But if Bernie can convince just one or 2%
of the people in the audience, it's worthwhile

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:36.100
and he could reach people that otherwise we'll
never have anything break their echo chamber,

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:40.840
pierce their propaganda, uh, and therefore
it's worth Bernie appearing both of respectable

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.690
and defensible points of view.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:45.150
So again, both are legitimate strategies.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.780
Each candidate should handle it, how they
see fit.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.880
They don't, oh, Fox News, anything.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.950
Their calculation should be, what do they
want to do?

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.430
How do they want to use Fox News if at all,
to push their agenda and to push their platform.

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:01.850
Uh, and if they don't want to do it, that's
perfectly reasonable.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:06.090
Now there will be all of the normal responses
to Elizabeth Warren's decision that we can

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.180
imagine.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:13.700
And we would expect Elizabeth Warren is scared
or she's avoiding debates and town halls.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.409
Well, Elizabeth Warren has done endless town
halls and she's faced countless questions.

00:04:18.409 --> 00:04:25.330
She recently took questions completely unprepared
when her plane from, I believe it was a DC

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.930
or LaGuardia to Charleston, I believe it was,
got very, very delayed.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.310
She held an impromptu town hall.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.479
She's faced questions from adversarial people.

00:04:33.479 --> 00:04:39.129
And people on her side saying that in particular
she believes Fox News is a bad faith actor,

00:04:39.129 --> 00:04:44.430
is very different than saying she's afraid
of or won't participate in town halls or adversarial

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:45.680
interviews.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:50.789
You also have to consider, and this is something
that I've not seen, uh, talked about since

00:04:50.789 --> 00:04:56.750
the story broke, given how poorly the Bernie
Sanders town hall went for Fox News.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:01.180
I mean a room full of people clapping for
Medicare for all a and clapping for Bernie

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.809
Sanders on Fox News.

00:05:02.809 --> 00:05:04.770
That's not great for Fox News.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:06.110
I would be shocked.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:12.330
A Fox allowed an Elizabeth Warren town hall
to go the same way that the Bernie Sanders

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.870
town hall went.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:19.960
My guess is that they would be much more prepared
to really make her look bad in a way that

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.210
they were unable to make Bernie Sanders look
bad.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:28.020
Now, Elizabeth Warren is smart and quick enough
that she still would probably do okay.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:33.830
But I think that that's also probably a consideration
in the last seven days as you may have noticed,

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:37.889
I have been pushed more and more in the direction
of Elizabeth Warren.

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:42.110
Um, I still find her quite uncharismatic on
a personality level.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:48.270
I don't see her really connecting with large
swaths of voters particularly well, but as

00:05:48.270 --> 00:05:54.259
I told you yesterday, her policy proposals
or detailed most of them I agree with, although

00:05:54.259 --> 00:05:57.080
I have some questions, uh, about some of them.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:01.819
And since the fiasco that was the handling
of her DNA test, she has been making many

00:06:01.819 --> 00:06:07.371
of the right decisions and I would be glad
to vote for her against Donald Trump and I

00:06:07.371 --> 00:06:10.819
would be glad to vote for Bernie Sanders against
Donald Trump as well.

00:06:10.819 --> 00:06:15.941
Uh, many similarities between the two important
differences, which we've discussed, but there

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:21.569
are some significantly a good candidates that
are running right now on, on the democratic

00:06:21.569 --> 00:06:26.719
side and good for Elizabeth Warren and this
entire book, by the way, this may have inadvertently

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:34.089
had the very successful popularizing of the
term hate for profit racket about Fox News,

00:06:34.089 --> 00:06:39.069
which has sort of instantly been mainstreamed,
um, and has appeared in all sorts of articles

00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:40.069
and commentaries.

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:42.469
So good for Elizabeth Warren.

00:06:42.469 --> 00:06:43.529
Good for Bernie Sanders.

00:06:43.529 --> 00:06:47.659
I respect both of their decisions, but I would
like to hear from you.

00:06:47.659 --> 00:06:51.800
Do you think Elizabeth Warren is making the
correct decision given all of the circumstances

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.580
or would you rather see her?

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:57.120
Do you think it would be the right decision
for her to do the Fox News?

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.120
Yeah,

00:06:58.120 --> 00:06:59.120
town hall.

